'faqs'=>[['Is premarital counselling only for couples with problems?','No. Couples also attend to discuss expectations, strengthen communication and identify decisions that deserve attention before marriage rather than during a later crisis.'],['Will the counsellor tell us whether to marry?','No. A counsellor should help you understand patterns, differences, agreements and concerns. The decision to marry remains with the two people involved.'],['Do parents attend premarital counselling?','Premarital counselling usually centres the couple. Family sessions may occasionally be discussed with both partners&rsquo; consent, but confidentiality and purpose should remain clear.'],['How many premarital sessions do couples need?','The number varies with goals and concerns. An initial session can define priorities, after which the therapist should discuss a suitable structure and review point.']],
